  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S Baba Biryani, Kanpur Thru. ... vs State Of U.P. Thru. Addl. Chief/Prin. ... on 21 March, 2023 Bench: Rajan Roy, Manish Kumar High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Court No. - 3 Case :- Writ - C No. - 1758 of 2023 Petitioner :- M/S Baba Biryani, Kanpur Thru. Proprietor Mahfooz Umar And Another Respondent :- State Of U.P. Thru. Addl. Chief/Prin. Secy. Deptt. Food Safety, Civil Secr Counsel for Petitioner :- Syed Ali Rehan,Mohd. Mansoor",
    "facts": "(iv) Allow the writ petition with costs in favour of the petitioners.\"",
    "arguments": "(iv) Issue any other writ, order or direction which this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper under the circumstances of the case. On being confronted, learned counsel for the petitioner submitted that this is a recommendation which would be taken into consideration by the Commissioner, Food Safety and Drugs Administration at Lucknow for grant of sanction under Section 30(2)(e) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Learned Additional Chief Standing Counsel says that sanction for prosecution has been granted and based thereon prosecution has been launched before the Chief Metropolitan Magistrate, Kanpur Nagar.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "On being confronted, learned counsel for the petitioner submitted that this is a recommendation which would be taken into consideration by the Commissioner, Food Safety and Drugs Administration at Lucknow for grant of sanction under Section 30(2)(e) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Learned Additional Chief Standing Counsel says that sanction for prosecution has been granted and based thereon prosecution has been launched before the Chief Metropolitan Magistrate, Kanpur Nagar.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "(iv) Issue any other writ, order or direction which this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper under the circumstances of the case."
  },
